  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Cell counts, Cellpose vs refined"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1100x440 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "if len(summary) and \"cellpose_n\" in summary:\n",
    "    fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax[0].scatter(summary[\"cellpose_n\"], summary[\"refined_n\"], s=18, alpha=.7)\n",
    "    lim = [0, max(summary[\"cellpose_n\"].max(), summary[\"refined_n\"].max()) * 1.05]\n",
    "    ax[0].plot(lim, lim, \"k--\", lw=.8, label=\"y = x\")\n",
    "    ax[0].set(xlabel=\"Cellpose cells\", ylabel=\"Refined cells\", xlim=lim, ylim=lim,\n",
    "              title=\"Cells per FOV\")\n",
    "    ax[0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax[1].hist(summary[\"delta_n\"], bins=25, color=\"steelblue\")\n",
    "    ax[1].axvline(0, color=\"k\", ls=\"--\", lw=.8)\n",
    "    ax[1].set(xlabel=\"refined - cellpose\", ylabel=\"FOVs\", title=\"Change in cell count\")\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Cell-area distributions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 770x440 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def areas(lab):\n",
    "    _, c = np.unique(lab[lab > 0], return_counts=True)\n",
    "    return c\n",
    "\n",
    "cp_areas, ref_areas = [], []\n",
    "for p in pairs:\n",
    "    _, cp, ref, _ = load_pair(p)\n",
    "    if cp is not None:\n",
    "        cp_areas.append(areas(cp))\n",
    "    ref_areas.append(areas(ref))\n",
    "\n",
    "cp_areas  = np.concatenate(cp_areas)  if cp_areas  else np.array([])\n",
    "ref_areas = np.concatenate(ref_areas) if ref_areas else np.array([])\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 4))\n",
    "bins = np.linspace(0, np.percentile(np.concatenate([cp_areas, ref_areas]), 99), 60)\n",
    "if len(cp_areas):\n",
    "    ax.hist(cp_areas, bins=bins, alpha=.55, label=f\"Cellpose (n={len(cp_areas)})\")\n",
    "ax.hist(ref_areas, bins=bins, alpha=.55, label=f\"Refined (n={len(ref_areas)})\")\n",
    "ax.set(xlabel=\"cell area (px)\", ylabel=\"cells\", title=\"Area distribution\")\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. What actually changed — IoU matching\n",
    "\n",
    "Matches Cellpose cells to refined cells by overlap, then classifies every cell:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **matched** — one-to-one, the refinement kept it\n",
    "- **split** — one Cellpose cell became several refined cells\n",
    "- **merged** — several Cellpose cells became one refined cell (the veto step)\n",
    "- **lost** — a Cellpose cell with no refined counterpart (e.g. removed as holey)\n",
    "- **gained** — a refined cell with no Cellpose counterpart\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the most informative view: cell *counts* alone can't tell a split from a\n",
    "lost cell plus a gained one."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
